4\t   share kind (integer, float64, decimal, rational), and within kind the\n   565\t   float zero sign, the decimal scale and the exact value; host integer\n   566\t   width is not significant, and canonical NaNs are equal (every NaN has\n   567\t   the one canonical encoding). Collections recurse the way equiv does,\n   568\t   metadata ignored. Unlike equiv, (content= 1 1.0) is false.\"\n   569\t  [a b]\n   570\t  (or (identical? a b)\n   571\t      (= (content-key a) (content-key b))))\n   572\t\n   573\t\n   574\t(defn content-hash\n   575\t  \"A hash consistent with content=. Host-specific like num-hash: never\n   576\t   compare hash values across hosts.\"\n   577\t  [x]\n   578\t  (hash (content-key x)))\n   579\t\n   580\t\n   790\t      (refuse :equality-collapse))\n   791\t    wired))\n   792\t\n   793\t\n   794\t(defn- map-bytes\n   795\t  \"A map at depth d; keys and values one level deeper.\"\n   796\t  [m d]\n   797\t  (deep! d :unsupported-value)\n   798\t  (let [wired (members-bytes (seq m) false :duplicate-key (inc d))\n   799\t        sorted (sort #(compare-canonical-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) wired)\n   800\t        pair-buffers (mapcat (fn [[kb _ vb]] [kb vb]) sorted)]\n   801\t    (concat-buffers (cons (write-head 5 (count wired)) pair-buffers))))\n   802\t\n90:width, `:canonical` uses bytewise key ordering and shortest numeric forms,\n91:and `:canonical-rfc7049` uses length-first ordering. Option precedence over\n153:vectors, finite lists/sequences, maps, sets, metadata, integers,\n155:qualified: it means the encoder accepts the value once its metadata is\n158:reader-position projection can reattach such metadata. Reject arbitrary\n183:  identifier components and metadata; normal astral text and noncharacters\n189:- Preserve collection and symbol metadata using Boring's `clojure/with-meta`\n191:  metadata. Clear metadata on internally constructed Dart collections\n192:  before attaching supplied metadata. Do not strip arbitrary user `:tag`\n